From e200502abe478d2cd2d604e75f9c2b0173d6fd44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:56:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0146 -- GUS voice-setup call cost diagnostic
 (S7-GUS)

WHY: dosags real hardware (tags GUST1/GUSD1, tests/games/trilbysnotes/
results/S7-gus-getstate-cost-realhw-2026-09-15.md) exonerated
SDL_DOSGusGetState() (patch SDL/0145) -- 28 calls, 27-170us each, ~3ms
total -- and instead found the MIDI slot Poll() loop's own 6.9s max is
ONE single call, nearly identical across two independent runs (175us
apart out of 6.89 SECONDS), pointing at a deterministic mechanism tied
to the song/scene content rather than I/O jitter or call-volume
aggregation. gus_sink.c's sink_note_on() calls SDL_DOSGusSetVoiceFreq,
SetVoiceVol, SetVoicePan, and SDL_DOSGusStartVoice once each per real
note-on; SDL_DOSGusStopVoice is called from reap_finished_voices(),
sink_note_off(), and allocate_voice()'s LRU-steal path. All five were
read this session -- every one is a bounded handful of outportb()/
inportb() calls, cli/sti-wrapped, with no retry/poll loop anywhere in
their own call graph (gus_select_voice, gus_w8, gus_w16, gus_hz_to_fc,
gus_linear_to_logvol, gus_encode_addr all checked) -- but that was also
true of SDL_DOSGusGetState() before it was measured, and this file's
own SDL_DOSMpu401WaitDRR/SDL/0093 precedent shows a single outportb/
inportb CAN cost far more than source reading predicts on a real ISA
bus, regardless of loop structure. Per this hub's "instrument the thing
that produces the unexplained quantity, not its neighbors" rule,
applied for the third time in this sub-investigation.

WHAT: brackets all five functions with uclock()-based microsecond
timestamps, one accumulate-and-snapshot pair per function, same idiom
as SDL_DOSGusGetState() (patch SDL/0145) this mirrors -- five
independent Diag Snapshot accessors so a caller can tell exactly which
one (if any) is responsible, not just their combined total.
SDL_DOSGusStopVoice is a real addition beyond the four functions
originally flagged for this pass (SetVoiceFreq/Vol/Pan/StartVoice): it
sits in the same reap/note-off call graph, is equally unmeasured, and
costs nothing extra to add to the same real-hardware run. dosags
patches/ags/0070 is the consumer.

Temporary -- to be reverted once this sub-investigation concludes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VVzc2V3qXnVbYZC693CTWt
